  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n\nThe central idea is to use a block-coordinate descent method with smooth optimization in eigenbasis domains to enforce periodicity constraints, a signature characteristic of the optimal solution to the minimum overlap problem. Unlike previous approaches that rely on arbitrary function representations, we leverage the mathematical property that solutions to the minimum overlap problem inherently possess periodic structure. This allows us to reduce the problem dimensionality by establishing periodicity constraints based on frequency analysis. The basis for this approach comes from harmonic analysis and the observation that the minimum overlap solution can be represented as a periodic function.\n\nThe algorithm will work by:\n- First identifying the function's spectral properties through FFT\n- Projecting the function into eigenbasis components\n- Optimizing each eigenbasis component separately against a smooth_curriculum objective while maintaining:\n    - Non-negativity constraints\n    - Integral constraint\n    - Periodicity requirements\n- Combining the optimized components to form the final solution\n\nLimitations:\n- This approach is computationally intensive due to spectral methods and optimization\n- The need for periodicity projection may discard potentially valuable non-periodic solutions\n- The smooth_curriculum parameter may require careful tuning\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n\nVariables:\n- Let h(x) be the step function to optimize, defined over [0,2]\n- Spectral projection: transform h(x) into frequency domain using FFT\n- Eigenbasis: obtain orthogonal periodic components using Fourier modes\n- Smooth_curriculum objective: minimize the maximum correlation between h and 1-h over all translations\n- Constraint formulation:\n  - Periodicity requirement: h(x+P) = h(x) + 0 (for all x) where P is period length\n  - Integral constraint: \u222bh(x)dx = 1\n  - Boundary constraints: 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1\n\nObjective function for block-coordinate descent:\n- We use: C5 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- For numerical efficiency: compute using FFT correlation\n- Smooth equivalent: C5_smooth = smooth_max(compute_correlation(h), alpha)\n\nConstraint handling:\nEach eigenbasis component is optimized under:\n- Individual non-negativity constraints\n- Coupled periodic projection\n- Transformed integral constraints\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n\nImplementation steps:\n\na. Phased optimization initialization:\n  1. Given input h_values, initialize arrays: \n      n_points = len(h_values)\n      grid = np.linspace(0,2,n_points)\n  2. Add cache\u0e2a\u0e33\u0e04\u0e31\u0e0d for FFT computations\n  3. Apply periodicity-based initialization using FFT\n\nb. Spectral projection loop:\n  1. Compute FFT of h_values\n  2. Identify frequency components\n  3. Project onto eigenbasis: construct basis functions that enforce periodicity\n  4. Initialize optimization variables for each basis component\n\nc. Block-coordinate descent:\n  For each iteration:\n      1. Select eigenbasis component q (from 1 to floor((n_points+1)/2))\n      2. Project constraint onto smooth_curriculum objective\n      3. Optimize component q separately using constrained minimization:\n          - Constraints: 0\u2264\u03d5\u22641 and periodic_component=base_q\n          - Objective: -\u222b|sin(\u03c9x + \u03c6)|\u00b2dx + \u03bb||\u03d5||\u2082\u00b2\n      4. Update global h(x) by combining optimized components\n\nd. Component-wise optimization:\n  For each component q:\n      x0 = initial_guess\n      bounds = np.array([[0,1]]*n_points)\n      constraints = [PeriodicityConstraint(), \n                    IntegralConstraint(target_sum = n_points/2)]\n      min_objective = minimize_periodic_part(...)\n\ne. Hierarchical recovery:\n  After completing all components:\n      - Project to feasible solution space\n      - Verify smooth_curriculum objective\n      - Re-evaluate entire function using true correlation metric\n      - If improved, commit solution\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**\n\nKey choices:\n\nEigenbasis projection:\n- Use real Fourier basis for efficiency: \u03c6_k(x) = sqrt(2/\u03c0) * cos(2\u03c0*k*x/P) for k=0,...,floor((n_points+1)/2)\n- Adjustable period length P based on grid resolution\n- Smooth_curriculum parameter \u03b1 starting from 10 and increasing by factor of 2 until improvement stalls\n\nOptimization strategy:\n- Constrained optimization for each eigenbasis component:\n  Objective: -|C5_smooth| + \u03b3*||\u03d5||\u2082\u00b2\n  Parameters:\n    \u03b1 \u2208 [50, 500, 1000, 5000] (smooth_curriculum variance)\n    \u03b3 \u2208 [0.01, 0.1, 0.2] (regularization terms)\n- Use IPOPT solver with bounds and periodicity constraints\n- Check convergence and acceptable gradient norm\n\nPeriodicity enforcement:\n- Use spectral filtering: zero-out frequency bands that violate period constraints\n- Projection matrix based on frequency signature rectification\n\nFallback mechanisms:\n- If no improvement over 5 iterations, switch to random restart\n- Maintain at least the current best solution if global optimum not found within time limits\n- Biased toward periodic solutions (all eigenvectors must be periodic)\n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**\n\nPhased execution:\n\nPhase 1 (Initialization and Preprocessing): 100 seconds\n  - Load initial_h_values\n  - Perform base dimensionality reduction\n  - Create initial optimization state\n\nPhase 2 (Eigenbasis optimization): 800 seconds (core optimization)\n  - Iterate over major components\n  - Tight coupling between eigenvector projection and smooth_curriculum optimization\n  - Introduce warm restart with increasing \u03b1\n\nPhase 3 (Secondary optimization): 200 seconds\n  - Refine minor components\n  - Full correlation check and hedging iterations\n  - Preparation for resolution projection\n\nTermination conditions:\n- Time exceeds budget\n- Function value improvement < 1e-6 for 3 consecutive iterations\n- Regularization becomes infeasibly large (> 10000)\n- User termination interrupt\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**\n\nFinalization Steps:\n  - Verify proper scaling: sum(h) == n/2\n  - Confirm periodicity: residue_levels < args.tolerance\n  - Compute final C5 using correlation function\n  - Format return value as (h_values, final_score, n_points)\n\nValidation checks:\n  T\u1ea5t c\u1ea3 \u0111i\u1ec3m: gi\u1eefa (sum) = n/2\n  T\u1ea5t c\u1ea3 h_i \u2208 [0,1]\n  C5 < current record\n  Smoothing is self-consistent with regularization parameter\n\nSanity checks:\n  Re-compute correlation using true integral sum\n  Check projection metadata matches grid\n  Validate at least one eigenbasis component improved",
